            <div xml:id="d244-a1">

                <pb facs="0400" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg306"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 462.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Decision of the Treasury Department concerning
                        stowaways.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Treasury Department,<lb/>Office of Superintendent of
                                Immigration</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                            C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1893-06-18"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">June 18, 1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your letter, in regard to
                    stowaways, of the 12th instant, and asking instructions concerning same, will
                    say that all stowaways who are aliens and arriving in vessels from foreign ports
                    must be treated as alien immigrants, and vessels bringing them will be liable to
                    all pains and penalties contained in the immigration laws. Any other
                    construction of the law would enable steamship companies to circumvene the same,
                    which requires all persons aboard their ships to be regularly manifested, and
                    stowaways will become quite numerous. Therefore, in the case of any unmanifested
                    alien immigrant you will proceed, if detained for special inquiry, to require
                    the four inspectors to decide upon their cases as in the case of all other
                    immigrants.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herman Stump</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Superintendent.</hi></signed><lb/><signed>Dr. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">J. H. Senner</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Commissioner of Immigration, Ellis Island, N.
                            Y.</hi></signed><lb/>Approved:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >J. G. Carlisle</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
